From 8199dc359bf1715a1488419fa704279b11e84b98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:40:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Verifier V26: the caravan instructions' records against
 the kernel [skip ci]

The replay of DepositLot, ShipLot, WithdrawLot, SettleCustody and
ReconcileLot also compares the records the transaction logged (existing
kinds, frontier_abi::v2::log) with what the kernel's step gives:
LOT_INBOUND (sent, worn, from_lot), LOT_SHIPPED (sent, worn, to_lot,
order id, carrier), LOT_SETTLED (delivered, burned, destination gone)
and exactly the LOT_LOSS records of the lot (Worn, Burned,
DestinationGone with the vault's holder, Seized with the captor,
Raided with the taker). A record of that kind and key with another
payload, or a loss record the kernel does not give, is a FAIL; a
record not among those shown is not judged (UNVERIFIABLE: the logs
may be cut).

Tests: the records in every case, each dropped (not judged) and each
changed by one unit (FAIL), an extra loss (FAIL); through verify() with
the records as Program data lines, a reconciliation is a full match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
